[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1617187956","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1617187956","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1617187956,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5gZFR0","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-03T03:40:17Z","updated_at":"2023-07-03T03:40:17Z","body":"This raises a larger question about the handling of `null` especially in arrays. In some cases an array element of `null` might be acceptable, in others it isn't. The current Arlington data model only explicitly defines a Type of `null` if ISO 32000-2 mentions it.\r\n\r\nDictionary handling is covered by 7.3.7 \"_A dictionary entry whose value is **null** (see 7.3.9, \"Null object\") shall be treated the same as if the entry does not exist._\" so dictionaries will never have a `null` unless ISO 32000-2 explicitly mentions it or there is a glitch in the matrix (e.g. Table 207 for **Mac** and **Unix** entries).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1617187956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1617205600","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1617205600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1617205600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5gZJlg","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-03T03:50:26Z","updated_at":"2023-07-03T03:50:26Z","body":"In the case of `ArrayOfStructElem`, this applies to `StructTreeRoot` **K** and **ParentTree** (number tree) and `StructElem` **K** and **Ref** entries. Consideration for `null` is not mentioned anywhere so we need to clarify ISO 32000-2 _before_ any change is made to the Arlington data model. Also, need to be very careful about generalizing for `number-tree` or `name-trees`...\r\n\r\nThis is what existing [Errata #157](https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157) on PDF 2.0 seeks to clarify.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1617205600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1618281902","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1618281902","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1618281902,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5gdQWu","user":{"login":"bdoubrov","id":10971979,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTcxOTc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10971979?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov","html_url":"https://github.com/bdoubrov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdoubrov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-03T13:37:57Z","updated_at":"2023-07-03T13:37:57Z","body":"I'd still try to go for an argument for allowing `null` in `name-tree` and `number-tree` based on the following text from 7.9.6:\r\n\r\n> A name tree serves a similar purpose to a dictionary — associating keys and values\r\n[...]\r\n> The values associated with the keys may be objects of any type. Stream objects shall be specified by indirect object references (7.3.8, \"Stream objects\"). The dictionary, array, and string objects should be specified by indirect object references, and other PDF objects (**null objects**, numbers, booleans, and names) should be specified as direct objects.\r\n\r\nThe second part of this text explicitly allows null objects as values. And the first part implies that `null` as a value in the `name-tree` shall be treated in the same way as a `null` value in the dictionary. \r\n\r\nSame applies to `number-tree`. And the **ParentTree** in the **StructureTreeRoot** is a perfect example of an important use case, where `null` values are almost unavoidable if some structure elements are deleted from the document. ","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1618281902/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619404758","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1619404758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1619404758,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5ghifW","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-04T03:11:46Z","updated_at":"2023-07-04T03:11:46Z","body":"One of the issues in https://github.com/veraPDF/veraPDF-library/issues/1355 is that the _key_ in the `name-tree` is `null` and name tree keys are defined as \"_where each keyi shall be a string_\" and \"_The keys shall be sorted in lexical order_\". `number-tree` use slightly different wording for the key type (\"_each keyi is an integer_\" - \"is\" vs \"shall\") but the same wording for the sorting requirement (\"_The keys shall be sorted in numerical order_\").\r\n\r\nSo `name-tree`/`number-tree` keys cannot be `null` (fails \"shall be a string\"/\"is an integer\") and no allowance is made in either the lexical or numeric sorting algorithms for `null` keys - for example, whether they need to come first, last, or are skipped over entirely. And what would it mean if you had a `null` key but a non-`null` value??? Is that meaningful? (I note in https://github.com/veraPDF/veraPDF-library/issues/1355 that both the key and value are both `null`).\r\n\r\nISO 32000-2 definitely needs improvement in this area - and worthy of a separate Errata.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619404758/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619509215","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1619509215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1619509215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5gh7_f","user":{"login":"u-fischer","id":4047173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNDcxNzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4047173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer","html_url":"https://github.com/u-fischer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-04T05:20:17Z","updated_at":"2023-07-04T05:20:17Z","body":"@petervwyatt The keys in my example in the verapdf issue are not null. The key is the zero at the start, the value of this key is an array and  *inside* this array are then the null values.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619509215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619631905","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1619631905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1619631905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5giZ8h","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-04T07:02:03Z","updated_at":"2023-07-04T07:02:03Z","body":"Oh! Sorry - I didn't check the file and misunderstood... I just saw a long array of `null`! \r\n\r\nCertainly, name-/number-trees can have any object (including `null`) as a value as @bdoubrov noted above, but precisely which objects are valid for each name-/number-tree is dependent on what the specific requirements defined for the key that is the name-/number-tree. \r\n\r\nIn the case of logical structure, there are plenty of \"shall\" statements saying what the value needs to be but `null` is not mentioned anywhere that I can see. And clause 7.3.9 starts with a very clear \"_The null object has a type and value that are unequal to those of any other object._\" so I think a heavy dose of sprinkling \"... or null object\" in Tables 354 and 355 is required. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619631905/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619775638","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1619775638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1619775638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5gi9CW","user":{"login":"u-fischer","id":4047173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNDcxNzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4047173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer","html_url":"https://github.com/u-fischer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/u-fischer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-04T08:22:20Z","updated_at":"2023-07-04T08:22:20Z","body":"> so I think a heavy dose of sprinkling \"... or null object\" in Tables 354 and 355 is required.\r\n\r\nI don't think so. This is about the parent tree, and the relevant section is 14.7.5.4, \"Finding structure elements from content items\" which says\r\n\r\n> * For a content stream containing marked-content sequences that are content items, the value shall be an array of indirect references to the sequences’ parent structure elements. The array element corresponding to each sequence shall be found by using the sequence’s marked-content identifier as a zero-based index into the array.\r\n\r\n> NOTE Because marked-content identifiers serve as indices into an array in the structural parent tree, their assigned values need to be as small as possible to conserve space in the array\r\n\r\nI pondered a lot about this when implementing the tagging. The question is if every value in the array must be an  indirect references  to a structure element, which would imply that the MCID on a page must be numbered consecutively starting from 0. Or if the *as small as possible* in the note means that gaps in the numbering are allowed and if yes how to fill up the gaps (the **null** value is then a quite logical candidate). \r\n\r\nIn LaTeX I implemented a strict numbering, but as shown by the axes4 example this is not the case in other implementations. A strict numbering would probably be a large problem for applications which edit a PDF as they would have to renumber the marked content sequences when content is deleted. \r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1619775638/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1620192500","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1620192500","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90","id":1620192500,"node_id":"IC_kwDOD6ym4s5gkiz0","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-04T12:49:53Z","updated_at":"2023-07-04T12:50:12Z","body":"Exactly. The issue is with the statement \"_... the value shall be an array of indirect references to the sequences’ parent structure elements._\" which does not permit `null` as that is clearly not an IR to a parent struct elem.\r\n\r\nIt is good that it is raised and we can seek clarification - such as simply appending \"or null\" to that sentence.\r\n\r\nDo you happen to know if any popular implementations can be made to create a similar scenario, or do they renumber MCIDs?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1620192500/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/comments/1620262839","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/arlington-pdf-model/issues/90#issuecomment-1620262839","issue_url":"ht